{"role":"assistant","content":"## Ruling: structural-half + compiler witness is acceptable\n\nNo additional test-layer admission machinery is required.\n\nThe harness classifies an **already-produced outcome**; it is not the callable-admission boundary. Reimplementing `dsg__admitted?` or reconstructing private admission closures in the oracle would duplicate compiler internals and make the harness more brittle without establishing a stronger boundary.\n\nThe responsibility split is sound:\n\n- **Compiler:** authenticity of callable descriptors. `test-common-call-source-admission` explicitly rejects forged entries, copied entry/witness combinations, substituted witnesses, and payload-modified descriptors (`test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1319-1350`).\n- **Oracle:** structural recognition plus revalidation of fixture ID, declared call, message, script, payload, collection shape, completed executions, and the original `clojure.core/meta` marker.\n\nA same-call descriptor copied with an identical payload represents the same observed deviation claim. There is no additional semantic distinction for this classifier to enforce. Cross-call substitution is refused by the declared-call guard, while malformed structural representations are refused locally. This satisfies the brief’s forged-representation requirement without inventing a second admission implementation.\n\n## Final verdict: ACCEPT H3-0 for landing\n\nThe remaining declaration-scope, shape-control, and narrative issues are resolved. The supplied verification is internally consistent: 100 agreements, 2 recorded deviations, 2 upstream failures, 2 blocked fixtures, 107 credited and 58 unexercised arities, with only the retained gate-closure assertion failing.\n\nThis acceptance approves the **H3-0 bookkeeping/disposition repair**, not program closure: the kernel gate remains `:blocked`, and H3-1 follows."}
